summary:
- topic: Recognition of Departing Board Member
  text: The board thanked departing member Jennifer Kinney for her year of service,
    highlighting her thoughtful contributions and significant time commitment to committees
    like the 2040 Comprehensive Plan Committee.
- topic: Student-Led Scholarship Initiative
  text: SPHS senior Huck Charv presented his initiative to create and fund a scholarship
    for students to study abroad, inspired by a previous board discussion on equity.
    The board praised his generosity and proactive effort to support his peers.
- topic: High School Graduation Venue
  text: The board discussed moving the high school graduation ceremony to a larger,
    indoor venue to avoid weather-related cancellations and accommodate more family
    members. They decided to survey students and families for input on potential locations
    like the Cross Insurance Arena.
- topic: Snow Day Policy Update
  text: The Superintendent announced a return to traditional snow days, which will
    be added to the end of the school year, instead of using remote learning days
    for the first five instances of inclement weather. Teacher union representatives
    voiced concerns about the change and offered to collaborate on a better remote
    learning plan.
- topic: Union Contract Ratification
  text: The board unanimously ratified a new three-year contract with the South Portland
    School District ServiceEmployeesAssociationContract. Board members and the superintendent
    praised the collaborative and professional negotiation process that led to a fair
    agreement.
- topic: Tribute to Educators
  text: Board member Rosemarie DeAngelis read a lengthy, emotional tribute to past
    and present South Portland educators, sharing dozens of comments from a social
    media post where former students recalled teachers who made a significant impact
    on their lives.
- topic: Board Officer Nominations
  text: Nominations were made for the next board chair (Molly Schen) and vice-chair
    (Tandy Ratliff). The formal vote will take place at the inauguration meeting in
    December.
